==================== Instruction ====================
I want a webpage where I can browse and use text templates created by others. I should be able to view a template library (e.g., resumes, weekly reports, or meeting minutes), select a template, fill in the relevant information through a simple form, and preview the results. I also want to be able to submit my own templates in plain text or Markdown format, which will also appear in the template library. Each template should display basic information such as author and description. New features and constraints: 1. Support for template categorization and multi-dimensional searching, allowing filtering by template type, applicable scenarios, popularity, and update time; the search box supports fuzzy keyword matching and real-time associative suggestions; 2. Support for template favorites, with a favorites list for quick retrieval of frequently used templates; 3. Form filling and generation constraints: set required fields for forms, preventing content generation when required fields are not filled; restrict special characters in input content to avoid formatting errors in the generated text.
